        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx` by making the header row `<div>` (line 122) behave as an accessible button. I couldn't re-run the linter: running oxlint needed approval, and nobody was available to give it in this run.\n\n**What I changed:** I added these attributes to the header `<div>`, keeping the file's alphabetical attribute order:\n- `role=\"button\"` clears `no-static-element-interactions`.\n- An `onKeyDown` handler calls `openTrigger()` on Enter or Space, which clears `click-events-have-key-events`. It also calls `preventDefault()` so Space doesn't scroll the page.\n- `tabIndex={0}` lets keyboard users reach the row. Without it, an element with `role=\"button\"` would trigger the related `interactive-supports-focus` rule.\n- `aria-expanded={open}` tells screen readers whether the section is open or closed.\n\n**Why I didn't switch to a `<button>`:** Excalidraw passes `<h3>` labels into this component (`label={<h3>…</h3>}`), and a heading isn't allowed inside a `<button>`. A real button would also bring its own border, background and font styles, which would change how the row looks.\n\nClicking works exactly as before. The only new behaviour is that the row can now be focused with Tab and toggled from the keyboard. No other files, suppression comments or lint configuration were touched.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "A real button would also bring its own border, background and font styles, which would change how the row looks."
