        "finalMessage": "I replaced the `<div role=\"button\">` in `collapsible.tsx:122` with a real `<button type=\"button\">`, so `jsx-a11y/prefer-tag-over-role` should no longer fire. I couldn't re-run the linter: there's no oxlint or lint config in the directory, so the re-lint step will be the first real check.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Gone:** `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex={0}` and the `onKeyDown` handler. A native button is focusable on its own and fires `onClick` for Enter and Space, so it behaves the same as before.\n- **Kept:** `aria-expanded`, `className`, `onClick` and the flex layout styles.\n- **Added style resets** so the button looks like the old div: `background: \"none\"`, `border: \"none\"`, `color: \"inherit\"`, `font: \"inherit\"`, `padding: 0`, `textAlign: \"inherit\"` and `width: \"100%\"` (a div fills the row by default; a button doesn't).\n\n**Two things a person should check:**\n1. **Inline styles win over the class.** If whatever CSS `className` points to sets padding, background, border or colour on this header, the new inline resets will override it. Check the Stats panel header still looks right. If it doesn't, move those resets into the stylesheet.\n2. **A heading inside a button isn't valid HTML.** The component is called with `label={<h3>…</h3>}`, and a button may only contain inline-level content. Browsers display it fine, but screen readers may no longer announce the heading. The proper fix is to put the button inside the `<h3>`, which means changing how `label` is passed in at the call site. That's outside this file, so I left it.",
